  {"q_en":"Q.5 (a)_OR Enlist Methods of levelling and explain any one in detail. (03 marks)","marks_en":"03 marks","marks_gu":"૦૩ ગુણ","a_en":"""<p><strong>Methods:</strong> Simple, Differential (compound), Fly, Check, Profile (longitudinal + cross), Reciprocal, Precise.</p><p><strong>Fly levelling in detail:</strong> Rapid levelling to connect a BM to a distant point with only BS and FS (no IS), taking readings at change points to carry RL quickly. Used to establish temporary BM near site, check performed by returning. Accuracy moderate, speed high.</p>""",
   "a_gu":"""<p>Simple, differential, fly, check, profile, reciprocal — <strong>Fly:</strong> માત્ર BS/FS થી ઝડપી BM connect, temporary BM માટે.</p>"""},
  {"q_en":"Q.5 (b)_OR Explain Following terms with respect to Theodolite (1) Transiting (2) Face left observation (3) Line of Collimation (4) Trunnion axis (04 marks)","marks_en":"04 marks","marks_gu":"૦૪ ગુણ","a_en":"""<p><strong>(1) Transiting (Plunging):</strong> Rotating telescope 180° about horizontal axis to point opposite direction — reverses line of collimation for extending line or face left/right.</p><p><strong>(2) Face left observation:</strong> When vertical circle is on observer's left while sighting. Mean of face left + face right eliminates collimation and index errors.</p><p><strong>(3) Line of Collimation:</strong> Optical axis — objective centre to cross-hair intersection. Must be perpendicular to horizontal axis (collimation adjustment).</p><p><strong>(4) Trunnion (Horizontal) axis:</strong> Axis about which telescope tilts vertically, supported by A-frames. Must be perpendicular to vertical axis.</p>""",
   "a_gu":"""<p><strong>Transiting:</strong> telescope 180° vertical flip. <strong>Face left:</strong> circle ડાબે — mean થી error cancel. <strong>Collimation:</strong> optical axis. <strong>Trunnion:</strong> vertical tilt નો આડો અક્ષ.</p>"""},
